\b\f39\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670  }{\f39\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 Write a C++ program that contains a class \lquote myClass\rquote  having two data members of type int.
\par The class must have
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f10\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li792\ri0\widctlpar\tx792\faauto\ls4\rin0\lin792\itap0 {\f39\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 
A default constructor which must initialize all the data members to their meaningful values.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f10\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'b7\tab}A destructor with no implementation.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f10\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'b7\tab}Setter member functions to set all data members of class
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f10\insrsid15336604\charrsid12259670 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'b7\tab}Getter member functions to get all data members of class
